<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Western Thrace</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> is the region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nestos">Nestos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maritsa">Evros</a> rivers in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. Taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a>, it saw a short-lived Muslim-led provisional government in 1913, passed to Greece after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, and its Muslim minority was exempted from the population exchange of 1923.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/western-thrace.jpg" alt="Western Thrace" width="320" height="277" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SilentResident,Philly boy92 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_map_of_Thrace_(Greece).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
